OpenBMC evb-ast2600: enable MCTP + PLDM with an MCTP-over-serial link

Turns on the DMTF PMCI stack (Code Construct mctpd + OpenBMC pldmd) for the
QEMU ast2600-evb machine and brings up an MCTP-over-serial (DSP0253) link on
AST2600 UART1 so the BMC can talk PLDM Type 0 to an external endpoint (a
Zephyr QEMU instance) over a -serial unix: socket bridge.

Changes
  * meta-aspeed/conf/machine/evb-ast2600.conf
      require pldm.inc (chains mctp.inc) -> DISTRO_FEATURES += "mctp pldm",
      DISTROOVERRIDES += ":df-mctp:df-pldm"; IMAGE_INSTALL:append = " pldm".
      This pulls packagegroup-obmc-apps-dmtf-pmci (-> mctp) and pldm, and
      auto-attaches the kernel MCTP fragment (CONFIG_MCTP/_SERIAL) via the
      df-mctp override on linux-aspeed's SRC_URI.
  * meta-evb-.../recipes-phosphor/mctp/mctp_%.bbappend (+files)
      ship mctp-local.service (bus-owner) that runs "mctp link serial
      /dev/ttyS0", assigns EID 8, route 18, and SetupEndpoint; plus mctpd.conf.
  * meta-evb-.../recipes-kernel/linux/linux-aspeed_%.bbappend (+patch)
      df-mctp SRC_URI patch enabling AST2600 UART1 (alias serial0 ->
      /dev/ttyS0) in aspeed-ast2600-evb.dts; console stays on UART5/ttyS4.

Verified: bitbake obmc-phosphor-image succeeds (5854 tasks); manifest carries
mctp/pldm/pldmtool/libpldm0; squashfs ships mctpd, pldmd, pldmtool and the
mctp-local.service wired into mctpd.service.wants; kernel .config has
CONFIG_MCTP=y / CONFIG_MCTP_SERIAL=y; built DTB shows serial@1e783000 okay.

---

### meta-aspeed/conf/machine/evb-ast2600.conf (modified)
diff --git a/meta-aspeed/conf/machine/evb-ast2600.conf b/meta-aspeed/conf/machine/evb-ast2600.conf
index c30cb5c0..dda33163 100644
--- a/meta-aspeed/conf/machine/evb-ast2600.conf
+++ b/meta-aspeed/conf/machine/evb-ast2600.conf
@@ -16,6 +16,17 @@ SOCSEC_SIGN_ENABLE = "0"
 require conf/machine/include/ast2600.inc
 include conf/machine/include/obmc-evb-common.inc
 
+# Enable the DMTF PMCI stack (MCTP + PLDM). pldm.inc chains mctp.inc, which
+# turns on the df-mctp/df-pldm distro overrides. Those in turn make
+# packagegroup-obmc-apps-dmtf-pmci pull in the Code Construct mctp daemon and
+# the OpenBMC pldm daemon, and attach the kernel MCTP/MCTP_SERIAL config
+# fragment. Mirrors the meta-evb-fvp-base machine wiring.
+require conf/distro/include/pldm.inc
+
+IMAGE_INSTALL:append = " \
+    pldm \
+"
+
 SERIAL_CONSOLES = "115200;ttyS4"
 
 # AST2600 EVB has 64MB SPI flash

### new files under meta-evb/meta-evb-aspeed/meta-evb-ast2600 (recipes-phosphor + recipes-kernel)
diff --git a/meta-evb/meta-evb-aspeed/meta-evb-ast2600/recipes-kernel/linux/linux-aspeed/0001-aspeed-ast2600-evb-enable-uart1-for-mctp-serial.patch b/meta-evb/meta-evb-aspeed/meta-evb-ast2600/recipes-kernel/linux/linux-aspeed/0001-aspeed-ast2600-evb-enable-uart1-for-mctp-serial.patch
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..078359c3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/meta-evb/meta-evb-aspeed/meta-evb-ast2600/recipes-kernel/linux/linux-aspeed/0001-aspeed-ast2600-evb-enable-uart1-for-mctp-serial.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+From: HFM <hfm@example.com>
+Date: Mon, 7 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: aspeed: ast2600-evb: enable UART1 for MCTP serial
+
+The AST2600 EVB devicetree only enables UART5 (the console, ttyS4).
+To carry an MCTP-over-serial (DSP0253) link to an external endpoint we
+need a second UART exposed to userspace. QEMU's ast2600-evb model wires
+the second -serial chardev to UART1, which Linux enumerates as ttyS0
+(serial0 alias). Enable it so `mctp link serial /dev/ttyS0` has a device
+to attach to.
+
+Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ast2600-evb QEMU MCTP-serial demo config]
+
+Signed-off-by: HFM <hfm@example.com>
+---
+ arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-ast2600-evb.dts | 4 ++++
+ 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)
+
+diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-ast2600-evb.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-ast2600-evb.dts
+--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-ast2600-evb.dts
++++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-ast2600-evb.dts
+@@ -205,8 +205,12 @@
+ &uart5 {
+ 	// Workaround for A0
+ 	compatible = "snps,dw-apb-uart";
+ };
+ 
++&uart1 {
++	status = "okay";
++};
++
+ &i2c0 {
+ 	status = "okay";
+ };
diff --git a/meta-evb/meta-evb-aspeed/meta-evb-ast2600/recipes-kernel/linux/linux-aspeed_%.bbappend b/meta-evb/meta-evb-aspeed/meta-evb-ast2600/recipes-kernel/linux/linux-aspeed_%.bbappend
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..d599b716
--- /dev/null
+++ b/meta-evb/meta-evb-aspeed/meta-evb-ast2600/recipes-kernel/linux/linux-aspeed_%.bbappend
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+FILESEXTRAPATHS:prepend := "${THISDIR}/${PN}:"
+
+# Enable AST2600 UART1 (Linux /dev/ttyS0, alias serial0) on the EVB so it can
+# carry an MCTP-over-serial link to an external endpoint. QEMU's ast2600-evb
+# model routes the second -serial backend to UART1; the stock EVB devicetree
+# leaves UART1 disabled, so add a fragment that turns it on.
+SRC_URI:append:df-mctp = " file://0001-aspeed-ast2600-evb-enable-uart1-for-mctp-serial.patch"
diff --git a/meta-evb/meta-evb-aspeed/meta-evb-ast2600/recipes-phosphor/mctp/files/mctp-local.service b/meta-evb/meta-evb-aspeed/meta-evb-ast2600/recipes-phosphor/mctp/files/mctp-local.service
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..533df4cb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/meta-evb/meta-evb-aspeed/meta-evb-ast2600/recipes-phosphor/mctp/files/mctp-local.service
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+[Unit]
+Description=MCTP configuration for serial ttyS0 (AST2600 UART1)
+After=mctpd.service
+Before=pldmd.service
+BindsTo=mctpd.service
+
+[Service]
+Type=simple
+ExecStartPre=stty -F /dev/ttyS0 115200 litout -crtscts -ixon -echo raw
+ExecStart=mctp link serial /dev/ttyS0
+ExecStartPost=sleep 3
+ExecStartPost=mctp link set mctpserial0 up
+ExecStartPost=mctp addr add 8 dev mctpserial0
+ExecStartPost=mctp route add 18 via mctpserial0
+ExecStartPost=busctl call au.com.codeconstruct.MCTP1 /au/com/codeconstruct/mctp1/interfaces/mctpserial0 au.com.codeconstruct.MCTP.BusOwner1 SetupEndpoint ay 0
+
+[Install]
+WantedBy=mctpd.service
diff --git a/meta-evb/meta-evb-aspeed/meta-evb-ast2600/recipes-phosphor/mctp/files/mctpd.conf b/meta-evb/meta-evb-aspeed/meta-evb-ast2600/recipes-phosphor/mctp/files/mctpd.conf
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..03c46e6c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/meta-evb/meta-evb-aspeed/meta-evb-ast2600/recipes-phosphor/mctp/files/mctpd.conf
@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+# Mode: either bus-owner, endpoint or unknown
+mode = "bus-owner"
+
+# MCTP protocol configuration. Used for both endpoint and bus-owner modes.
+[mctp]
+message_timeout_ms = 5000
diff --git a/meta-evb/meta-evb-aspeed/meta-evb-ast2600/recipes-phosphor/mctp/mctp_%.bbappend b/meta-evb/meta-evb-aspeed/meta-evb-ast2600/recipes-phosphor/mctp/mctp_%.bbappend
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..14948b17
--- /dev/null
+++ b/meta-evb/meta-evb-aspeed/meta-evb-ast2600/recipes-phosphor/mctp/mctp_%.bbappend
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+FILESEXTRAPATHS:prepend := "${THISDIR}/files:"
+
+# Bring up an MCTP-over-serial (DSP0253) link on the AST2600 EVB so the BMC
+# can speak PLDM to an external endpoint reachable over a UART. The second
+# QEMU -serial backend is wired to AST2600 UART1, which Linux exposes as
+# /dev/ttyS0 (serial0 alias). Modeled on meta-evb-fvp-base.
+SRC_URI:append = " \
+  file://mctp-local.service \
+  file://mctpd.conf \
+"
+
+SYSTEMD_SERVICE:${PN} += "mctp-local.service"
+
+do_install:append() {
+    install -m 0644 ${UNPACKDIR}/mctp-local.service ${D}${systemd_system_unitdir}/
+    install -d ${D}/etc/
+    install -m 0644 ${UNPACKDIR}/mctpd.conf ${D}/etc/mctpd.conf
+}
